WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.060
- [Narrator] Americans are
heading to the polls after weeks

00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:04.783
of record setting early voting.

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:07.940
Key battleground states
could decide who wins

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:10.440
the presidential race between
President Donald Trump

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:13.450
and former Vice President Joe Biden.

00:00:13.450 --> 00:00:15.540
And some states are just now beginning

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:17.800
to count a flood of mail-in ballots,

00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:21.110
meaning election results could
take days to be announced.

00:00:21.110 --> 00:00:25.360
- We will make America great again.

00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:27.150
Thank you Pennsylvania.
(crowd cheering)

00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:28.890
Thank you, Pennsylvania.

00:00:28.890 --> 00:00:31.320
- I'm running as a proud Democrat

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:35.570
but I will govern as an American president

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:39.310
- [Narrator] After an
unprecedented campaign season,

00:00:39.310 --> 00:00:42.370
election day 2020 has finally arrived

00:00:42.370 --> 00:00:44.980
with both candidates
offering dueling visions

00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:46.630
for the nation's future.

00:00:46.630 --> 00:00:48.970
Trump has pledged to
be a political outsider

00:00:48.970 --> 00:00:50.890
who will bring the economy back,

00:00:50.890 --> 00:00:53.070
while Biden pitched himself as a president

00:00:53.070 --> 00:00:55.530
who can unite a divided country.

00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:57.960
Months of preparations
to hold a safe election

00:00:57.960 --> 00:01:00.830
and tabulate early votes
will be put to the test,

00:01:00.830 --> 00:01:03.150
capping a race that has
largely been defined

00:01:03.150 --> 00:01:05.340
by the coronavirus pandemic.

00:01:05.340 --> 00:01:08.020
Many States have already
seen historic levels

00:01:08.020 --> 00:01:11.100
of early voting and more
than two thirds of responders

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:14.400
in the latest National
WSJ/NBC News poll said,

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:18.490
they plan to vote early
either by mail or in person

00:01:18.490 --> 00:01:21.070
- You're too have a duty, a duty to vote.

00:01:21.070 --> 00:01:22.530
- [Narrator] Polls
indicate that supporters

00:01:22.530 --> 00:01:25.295
of Biden are more likely
to have voted early.

00:01:25.295 --> 00:01:26.720
(crowd shouting)

00:01:26.720 --> 00:01:28.660
While supporters of Trump are more likely

00:01:28.660 --> 00:01:30.860
to vote in person on election day.

00:01:30.860 --> 00:01:33.510
- Get your friends, get your
family, get your neighbors,

00:01:33.510 --> 00:01:35.360
get your coworkers, get your boss,

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:37.422
grabbed him by the tie
say, "Let's go boss."

00:01:37.422 --> 00:01:38.255
(crowd laughing)

00:01:38.255 --> 00:01:40.090
And get out and vote.

00:01:40.090 --> 00:01:43.060
- [Narrator] Turnout will
also impact other key races.

00:01:43.060 --> 00:01:45.470
Republicans are defending
their senate majority

00:01:45.470 --> 00:01:46.730
which is up for grabs

00:01:46.730 --> 00:01:49.990
as 14 seats are now
considered competitive.

00:01:49.990 --> 00:01:51.640
And Democrats are working to hold

00:01:51.640 --> 00:01:53.530
and expand their majority in the house,

00:01:53.530 --> 00:01:55.763
particularly in suburban districts.

00:01:56.790 --> 00:01:57.870
(upbeat music)

00:01:57.870 --> 00:01:59.930
And keep an eye on the battleground states

00:01:59.930 --> 00:02:02.050
that could decide the presidential race.

00:02:02.050 --> 00:02:03.340
- Hello, Wisconsin.

00:02:03.340 --> 00:02:04.173
We're back.

00:02:04.173 --> 00:02:06.420
We're back, we gotta win.

00:02:06.420 --> 00:02:08.760
- Ohio, one more day.

00:02:08.760 --> 00:02:10.503
- Well, hello Pennsylvania.

00:02:11.381 --> 00:02:12.881
- What's up Miami.

00:02:13.930 --> 00:02:14.970
- [Narrator] Key states to watch,

00:02:14.970 --> 00:02:18.000
include the Western States
of Nevada and Arizona.

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:19.970
The Midwestern State of Iowa,

00:02:19.970 --> 00:02:23.910
Southern States, Texas, Georgia,
Florida and North Carolina.

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:26.650
And perhaps most importantly,
the Great Lake States

00:02:26.650 --> 00:02:30.550
of Wisconsin, Michigan,
Ohio and Pennsylvania.

00:02:30.550 --> 00:02:32.090
That's where the candidates held most

00:02:32.090 --> 00:02:34.920
of their events in the
final hours of the campaign.

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:37.860
- I've gotten to know
this state very well.

00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:38.693
You know, you surprise,

00:02:38.693 --> 00:02:40.410
you know you're the one
that put us over the top,

00:02:40.410 --> 00:02:41.243
you know that, right?

00:02:41.243 --> 00:02:42.450
Remember.
(crowd cheering)

00:02:42.450 --> 00:02:45.310
- Pennsylvania, 2008 and 2012,

00:02:45.310 --> 00:02:48.250
you placed your trust in Barack and me.

00:02:48.250 --> 00:02:52.380
Now in 2020, I'm asking
for your trust again.

00:02:52.380 --> 00:02:53.380
- [Narrator] Well, the most recent,

00:02:53.380 --> 00:02:56.490
WSJ/NBC News national poll shows Joe Biden

00:02:56.490 --> 00:02:58.130
with a 10 point lead.

00:02:58.130 --> 00:03:00.880
The race could hinge on states
that President Trump flipped

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:03.410
by slim margins four years ago.

00:03:03.410 --> 00:03:07.880
In 2016, Trump won Michigan
by less than 11,000 votes,

00:03:07.880 --> 00:03:10.870
Wisconsin by less than 23,000 votes

00:03:10.870 --> 00:03:13.820
and Pennsylvania by about 44,000 votes.

00:03:13.820 --> 00:03:16.170
- Put you ballot right over here.

00:03:16.170 --> 00:03:18.110
- [Narrator] And what about results?

00:03:18.110 --> 00:03:21.140
Well, we may get early clues
about the race from Florida,

00:03:21.140 --> 00:03:22.720
Ohio and North Carolina

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:25.870
where polls closed between
7 and 8:00 PM Eastern.

00:03:25.870 --> 00:03:27.010
It could take days

00:03:27.010 --> 00:03:29.200
to know the winner of
states like Pennsylvania,

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:31.240
Michigan and Wisconsin.

00:03:31.240 --> 00:03:33.070
That's because laws in those states say,

00:03:33.070 --> 00:03:35.850
election officials couldn't
count mail-in ballots ahead

00:03:35.850 --> 00:03:37.190
of this week.

00:03:37.190 --> 00:03:40.150
In some states ballots that
arrive after election day,

00:03:40.150 --> 00:03:42.730
may also be counted as
long as they're postmarked

00:03:42.730 --> 00:03:44.280
by November 3rd.

00:03:44.280 --> 00:03:47.170
The late tallying rules
have both parties preparing

00:03:47.170 --> 00:03:48.330
for legal battles.

00:03:48.330 --> 00:03:52.480
- We should know the result of
the election on November 3rd,

00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:54.429
the evening of November 3rd.

00:03:54.429 --> 00:03:55.510
(crowd cheering)

00:03:55.510 --> 00:03:57.870
That's the way it's been and
that's the way it should be.

00:03:57.870 --> 00:03:59.900
What's going on in this country?

00:03:59.900 --> 00:04:03.610
- I don't care how hard
Donald Trump tries.

00:04:03.610 --> 00:04:05.100
There's nothing, let me say that again.

00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:08.240
There's nothing that he
can do to stop the people

00:04:08.240 --> 00:04:10.900
in this station from voting
in overwhelming numbers

00:04:10.900 --> 00:04:12.802
and taking back this democracy.

00:04:12.802 --> 00:04:15.552
(crowd cheering)

